# PR/Issue Link + Auto Git Actions

When working on tracked GitHub work in the current session, always include a clickable Markdown link in every assistant message.

- If an active PR exists, include the PR link (preferred).
- If no PR exists but an active issue exists, include the issue link.
- Required formats:
  - `PR: [#<number>](https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/<number>)`
  - `Issue: [#<number>](https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<number>)`
- If multiple PRs exist, include the most recently opened active PR.
- If multiple issues exist and no PR exists, include the most recently active issue.
- Keep the required link present even in short status updates and acknowledgements.

## Commit/Push Behavior

- Do not ask whether to commit or push.
- After making requested code/rule changes for active work, create an appropriate commit and push the branch automatically.
